activitytrack-desktop (0.9.4~beta4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The app's 5-minute time grid next to the time fields: start and end by
    dragging or two clicks, the other activities hatched (web issue #38).
  * Settings → Generale: dates European, American or ISO, 24 or 12 hours;
    the command line and the terminal follow them.
  * A known client chosen brings its company.
  * On the library 0.9.4-beta4: resuming without concurrent entries
    suspends the others (app issue #132).

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:52:22 +0100

activitytrack-desktop (0.9.4~beta3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A Debian revision in the version, the distribution in it
    (0.9.4~beta3-1~deb13), on the library 0.9.4-beta3 that has it too:
    0.9.4~beta2~deb13 sorted before 0.9.4~beta2, so "python3-activitytrack
    (>= 0.9.4~beta2)" could not be satisfied. Source format 3.0 (quilt), as
    the revision wants. Nothing else changes.

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:57:02 +0100

activitytrack-desktop (0.9.4~beta2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The rules, the local copy and the sync come from the library
    python3-activitytrack, shared with the command line (activitytrack-cli)
    and the text interface (activitytrack-tui): one application, one data
    folder (~/.local/share/activitytrack), one pairing; what they do shows
    at once. The folder of 0.9.4-beta1 moves there at the first start.
  * Windows: the translations are in the bundle.

 -- ActivityTrack Desktop <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0100

activitytrack-desktop (0.9.4~beta1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reminders of the phone, as desktop notifications with their buttons:
    still working, still on pause, no activity at day start, a planned
    to-do coming, the planned end; each one can be switched off.
  * Windows: a per-user installer (not signed).
  * Generale: start at sign-in, daily check of newer releases on GitHub.
  * The interface in English, German and Spanish too.
  * User manual, it and en.

 -- ActivityTrack Desktop <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0100

activitytrack-desktop (0.9.3~alfa1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First test release (docs/DESIGN.md, phases 1-3).
  * Tray icon in the mode of the running activity, its commands in the
    menu; pairing with ActivityTrack Web by the web's link; sync both ways
    as a paired device, offline included.
  * Activities: quick entry, full form, stop sheet, times; free text in
    every field.
  * To-dos: the Home list with the app's filters, start, done, ignore,
    postpone, new and planned.

 -- ActivityTrack Desktop <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
